---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Why this site exists and how models are curated.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 py-12 max-w-prose">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink mb-8">About this site</h1>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">Why this exists</h2>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-500">
        Getting started with 3D printing is harder than it needs to be. Most guides assume you already know
        what a slicer is, or bury beginner advice inside enthusiast forums. This site ships the essentials —
        eight guides, ten models — and stops there. Workshop tone, no affiliate links, no padded word counts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">How models are curated</h2>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-500">
        Every model is license-verified (CC0, CC-BY, or CC-BY-SA) before it appears here. Difficulty is capped
        at intermediate. Each model teaches one specific skill. Models requiring proprietary slicers, exotic
        filaments, or enclosed enclosures are excluded from v0.1.0.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3">License + attribution</h2>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-500">
        Site code is MIT. Model files retain their original licenses — see each model detail page for the
        specific terms. Images are either original work or sourced under the Unsplash License. No real-name
        watermarks appear in any asset on this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 border-t border-neutral-100 pt-6 mt-10">
      — alienbushman, 2026
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
